law.text:
		An action affecting a conservation easement may be brought by:

An owner of an interest in real property burdened by the easement;


A holder of the easement;


A person having an express third-party right of enforcement;


The Attorney General of the Commonwealth;


The Virginia Outdoors Foundation;


The Virginia Historic Landmarks Board;


The local government in which the real property is located; or


Any other governmental agency or person with standing under other statutes or common law.
